The fixtures of the login-shell package's linked test
(packages/login-shell/LoginShellTest/Linked/LoginShell/Contract.lean and
.../Real.lean), which the linked test reads from this directory, the
package's tests/login-shell, and copies into each check's own temporary
directory. Both must stay executable (mode 100755). No check runs the
user's own shell or reads their profile.

- shell: stands for a login shell. `shell -l -c <command>` clears its
  environment, sources the file profile of the directory it runs in, which
  each check writes beside it (setting PATH, and printing noise), runs the
  command and prints noise before and after it. In a directory that holds
  the file fixture-fail it prints `login-shell fixture: failing here` on
  its standard error and exits 1.
- prepend: stands for a directory source such as mise. Run with no
  arguments, it prints `PATH=<the line in fixture-prepend>:<its PATH>`, so
  a child gets that directory first and the base's PATH after it.
